# Codex findings that share no source span with any other run's record (singleton groups; anchors are their own quotes)
CX X:BF-M-0014 | The dependency guard's documented command parser is minimal (no npx npm, no encoded PowerShell commands), so enforcement is narrower than the npm bypass rule.
RD OVERLAP X:BF-M-0014 P:RULE-M-0210 | P's hook record reports the same parser gaps (npx npm, -EncodedCommand) as exceptions of the PreToolUse block.
CX X:BF-M-0016 | The edit hook only enforces when the event carries a string file_path inside a resolvable checkout; other edit events finish silently.
CX X:BF-M-0018 | Hook change detection uses SHA-256 content identity but switches to size and modification time for files above 1 MiB.
CX X:BF-M-0019 | Hook state is persisted in an override directory, the Git directory or a temp folder, and failure to persist it is swallowed.
CX X:BF-M-0021 | The Stop co-change hook is skipped for recursive stops (stop_hook_active) and for unresolvable or non-Git environments.
RD OVERLAP X:BF-M-0021 P:EXTRA-M-0036 | P reports the Stop reminder is suppressed while stop_hook_active; X adds the non-Git / unresolvable-root skip.
CX X:BF-M-0022 | Repository-root resolution scopes checks through the common Git directory and template offset; nested unrelated repositories inside the template resolve to the template root.
CX X:BF-M-0032 | Project-reference checks classify projects only by file-name suffix; projects with other names are not classified.
CX X:BF-M-0070 | Arrange/Act/Assert is the default test structure; comments are optional when the phases are obvious.
